    {
      "name": "Note: everyone is asked",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Every customer is asked.** Each completed job gets one review request. Nothing in this workflow picks customers by how they felt about the job, and nothing should be added that does: Google does not allow asking only some customers for reviews. The text links straight to the business's Google review page (`review_link` in Config).",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "edc33001-7468-4895-e351-094c621a45ad",
      "position": [
        0,
        -380
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Note: wiring and swap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Trigger:** POST a JSON body `{job_id, customer_name, customer_mobile, customer_email, completed_at}` to this webhook when a job is marked complete. Any job tool that can send a webhook (ServiceM8, Tradify, simPRO, Fergus, AroFlo, Jobber) can be pointed at it, or upload a CSV and post one row per job.\n\n**Swapping the stand-in for a real SMS service (Twilio, ClickSend, MessageMedia):** in the \"Config\" node change `sms_api_url` to the provider's send-message URL, then on each \"Send ...\" HTTP Request node attach that provider's credential (an n8n credential you create, shown here as \"SMS provider (replace me)\") and adjust the JSON field names (`to`, `from`, `body`) to the provider's. The checks, duplicate handling and logging around it do not change.\n\nThe email step uses an n8n SMTP credential shown as \"Email (replace me)\".",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "6366c981-53d9-3e2c-422d-0976097768f9",
      "position": [
        560,
        -380
      ]
    },
